  m_Name: Beam
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonId: ' LESSON002'
  lessonTitle: BEAM BRIDGE
  lessonImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6aedd357aa978324690d88ed82a19beb, type: 3}
  popupDescription: A beam bridge is a simple bridge made of a <b><#E09500>horizontal
    deck or beam supported by piers or abutments</color></b>. The supports carry
    the bridge's weight and the loads traveling across it.
  almanacImage: {fileID: 0}
  lessonDescription: 'A beam bridge is a structural system consisting primarily of
    <b><#E09500>horizontal beams supported by piers, columns, or abutments</color></b>.
    When a downward load acts on the bridge, the beam bends, generally producing
    <b><#E09500>compression on one side and tension on the other</color></b>. These
    forces are carried through the structure toward its supports. Beam bridges are
    commonly suited to <b><#E09500>relatively short spans</color></b> because increasing
    the distance between supports increases the structural demands on the beam. '
